{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Neuron\/documentation\/Neuron\/WGANGP","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Neuron\/documentation\/Neuron\/WGANGP\/fakeLabel","doc:\/\/Neuron\/documentation\/Neuron\/WGANGP\/lambda","doc:\/\/Neuron\/documentation\/Neuron\/WGANGP\/lossFunction","doc:\/\/Neuron\/documentation\/Neuron\/WGANGP\/penaltyStepSize","doc:\/\/Neuron\/documentation\/Neuron\/WGANGP\/realLabel"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","generated":true}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/neuron\/wgangp"]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"title":"WGANGP","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"WGANGP","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"class","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WGANGP","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Class","externalID":"s:6Neuron6WGANGPC","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Neuron"}]},"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Neuron\/documentation\/Neuron\/GAN"],"title":"Inherits From","type":"inheritsFrom","kind":"relationships"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Neuron\/documentation\/Neuron"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"A Wasserstein GAN with Gradient Penalty (WGAN-GP) trainer.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WGANGP","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Enforces the Lipschitz constraint by penalizing ","type":"text"},{"code":"λ · (‖∇ₓD(x̂)‖ − 1)²","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on samples ","type":"text"},{"code":"x̂","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"interpolated between real and generated ones, instead of clipping weights.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The penalty’s gradient with respect to the critic’s parameters needs a second derivative,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"(∂\/∂θ ∇ₓD) · v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which Neuron’s first-order backward pass can’t produce. Mixed partials","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"commute, so it equals the change in the parameter gradient when the input moves along ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and one extra forward and backward pass at a perturbed input approximates it by finite","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"differences. See ","type":"text"},{"code":"gradientPenalty(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The perturbed pass must see the same critic as the unperturbed one, so the critic must be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deterministic in training mode: no ","type":"text"},{"code":"Dropout","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A fresh mask in each pass would be divided by the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"finite-difference step and swamp the penalty. ","type":"text"},{"code":"BatchNormalize","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" mixes samples, which the penalty","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(a per-sample norm) assumes they don’t; use ","type":"text"},{"code":"LayerNormalize","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"GroupNormalize","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in a critic.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://Neuron/documentation/Neuron/WGANGP/lambda":{"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"lambda","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Tensor","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Neuron6TensorC"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Scalar","kind":"typeIdentifier","pre